55,3,1,talk,Ryuji,,"The candidates are Language Learning Circles, Digital Archive Portal, Maker Workshop, and Mobile Branch Service. I vote against the Mobile service.","{""words"":21,""mentions"":[],""raw_differs"":false}"
56,3,1,talk,Yumi,,The Mobile Branch Service is exactly what the outer wards need since the buses are gone. I strongly support it.,"{""words"":20,""mentions"":[],""raw_differs"":false}"
57,3,1,talk,George,,The Mobile service is a budget trap. The Language Learning Circles seem more sustainable if they use partner organizations.,"{""words"":19,""mentions"":[],""raw_differs"":false}"
58,3,1,talk,May,,The Digital Archive failed once before. The Maker Workshop needs certification we don't have. I prefer the Language Circles.,"{""words"":19,""mentions"":[],""raw_differs"":false}"
59,3,1,talk,Daisuke,,The Maker Workshop sounds scary without a technician. Language Circles seem safer for the staff if partners help.,"{""words"":18,""mentions"":[],""raw_differs"":false}"
60,3,2,talk,Ryuji,,"I agree with George. Language Learning Circles rely on partner organizations, reducing our direct dependency and risk.","{""words"":17,""mentions"":[""George""],""raw_differs"":false}"
61,3,2,talk,Yumi,,"@George, @Ryuji, if we don't choose the Mobile service, we are abandoning the people who lost their bus links.","{""words"":19,""mentions"":[""George"",""Ryuji""],""raw_differs"":false}"
62,3,2,talk,George,,We can't provide a service that we have to cut in two years. That is worse than not starting it.,"{""words"":20,""mentions"":[],""raw_differs"":false}"
63,3,2,talk,May,,"@Yumi, the Language Circles can be coordinated across the district, potentially reaching those people through existing community hubs.","{""words"":18,""mentions"":[""Yumi""],""raw_differs"":false}"
64,3,2,talk,Daisuke,,I feel more comfortable with the Language Circles. It doesn't require specialized technical supervision from us.,"{""words"":16,""mentions"":[],""raw_differs"":false}"
65,3,3,talk,Ryuji,,It is the most rational choice given the grant terms and the staffing gaps Daisuke mentioned.,"{""words"":16,""mentions"":[""Daisuke""],""raw_differs"":false}"
66,3,3,talk,Yumi,,"I still feel it's not enough for the outer wards, but I see the budget point.","{""words"":16,""mentions"":[],""raw_differs"":false}"
67,3,3,talk,George,,It is a stable path. It avoids the vehicle overhead and the technical failures of the past.,"{""words"":17,""mentions"":[],""raw_differs"":false}"
68,3,3,talk,May,,It's a proven model—partner-run groups are the only things that lasted from six years ago.,"{""words"":15,""mentions"":[],""raw_differs"":false}"
69,3,3,talk,Daisuke,,I agree. It's the most sustainable for everyone.,"{""words"":8,""mentions"":[],""raw_differs"":false}"
